[617.598569, "o", "     1\t## Investigation Brief 05 — Meeting Amendments and Owners\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tCommittee ruling (binding for extract):\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\tCommittee minutes show owner churn from unsigned drafts. Ledger owner is the\r\n     6\tdefault. Meeting note amendments under `#### Amendment for TXN-<uuid>` replace\r\n     7\towner when `signed: true` (case insensitive) and, when the amendment includes\r\n     8\t`effective: YYYY-MM-DD`, only if that date is greater than or equal to the\r\n     9\tledger date for the transaction.\r\n    10\t\r\n    11\t## Investigation Brief 05 — Meeting Amendments and Owners — field notes\r\n    12\t\r\n    13\tDuring October count, R. Okonkwo circulated a draft finding on inventory obsolescence reserve. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n    14\t\r\n    15\tInterview #143 with operations finance highlighted how inventory obsolescence reserve statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel a"]
[617.598618, "o", "dvised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n"]
[617.617524, "o", "    16\t\r\n    17\tWorking paper WP-4980 documents a three-way match failure tied to inventory obsolescence reserve. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n    18\t\r\n    19\tLead reviewer S. Patel noted that inventory obsolescence reserve created reconciliation noise in operations finance during October count. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n    20\t\r\n    21\tThe committee packet references inventory obsolescence reserve as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n    22\t\r\n    23\tIn October count, external advisors reviewed inventory obsolescence reserve and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n    24\t\r\n    25\tRisk assessment WP-6"]
[617.617582, "o", "252 ties inventory obsolescence reserve to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\tWorking paper WP-1549 documents a three-way match failure tied to inventory obsolescence reserve. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\tIn October count, external advisors reviewed inventory obsolescence reserve and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n    30\t\r\n"]
